### Step 15: Configure Terraform backend in each module

```hcl
# modules/hub-network/backend.tf
terraform {
  backend "azurerm" {
    resource_group_name  = "rg-terraform-state"
    storage_account_name = "sttfstateprod"
    container_name       = "tfstate"
    key                  = "hub-network.tfstate"
  }
}
```

**Initialize with backend config:**

```bash
terraform init \
  -backend-config="resource_group_name=rg-terraform-state" \
  -backend-config="storage_account_name=sttfstateprod" \
  -backend-config="container_name=tfstate" \
  -backend-config="key=hub-network.tfstate"
```

**Why:**
- Separate state files per module reduce blast radius.
- Teams can work on different modules without blocking each other. [reddit](https://www.reddit.com/r/Terraform/comments/koz2ey/best_practice_for_remote_state_file_storage_in/)

